  "fault_schedule": "Five real memory-backed Go processes: drop completed START response, retry exact identity; one unavailable partition; native competing owner after close/reopen; terminal deletion and byte-capped global merge.",
  "assertions": [
    "Full unchanged pinned VisibilityPersistenceSuite passes through a genuine Temporal visibility manager and actual Go service processes.",
    "All seven attribute types, direct schema additions, CHASM aliases/divisions, four-partition keyset merge and fanout failure are checked.",
    "Terminal tombstones, index deletion, empty-vs-zero identity separation, durable outcome replay and fenced old-owner rejection survive reopening.",
    "Saved PostgreSQL Text expectations and exact integer/decimal/null semantics pass pure-Go tests."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Memory object-store component and process RPC proof; managed S3 topology, Temporal boot/Omes and real-S3 remain separate gates.",
    "The separate PostgreSQL oracle script executes the pinned host-specific ephemeral database fixture; saved oracle cases run in this portable Go manifest.",
    "Terminal deletion prevents same-run repair/reindex by design. Documents cap at2MiB, results at3MiB; journal retention remains bounded and no expiry is invented."
  ],
